  1. Identify the wiring diagram on the jack :: evidence: A close-up photo of the wiring diagram on the jack showing whether it reads T568A or T568B.
  2. Strip the blue cable's outer jacket :: evidence: Photo showing the blue jacket removed and four colour-coded twisted pairs visible, with no nicks on any inner wire.
  3. Untwist and straighten each pair :: evidence: Photo showing all eight individual wires straightened and lined up against the jack's colour-coded slots, not yet pressed in.
  4. Seat each wire into its correct jack slot :: evidence: Photo showing all eight wires lying in their correct colour-labelled slots, visible from above.
  5. Punch down all wires with the punch tool :: evidence: Photo showing all eight wire ends trimmed flush, with no excess wire sticking up above the jack body.
  6. Snap the cap onto the jack :: evidence: Photo showing the yellow cap fully closed and flat against the top of the jack.
  7. Snap the jack into the faceplate :: evidence: Photo showing the jack sitting flush and level in the faceplate with no gaps around its edges.
  8. Fold cable and mount faceplate to box :: evidence: Photo showing the faceplate sitting flat against the wall with the screw tightened and no cable pinched at the edges.
  9. Test the link with a cable tester :: evidence: Photo of the cable tester display showing all 8 lights passing (lit in order 1 through 8, with no lights missing or out of sequence).

